    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor phrasing/formatting differences (e.g., how the agent describes the diffstat) would not matter if the required information were delivered.\n\nCritical issues: (1) The agent did not inspect the first three PRs—only one PR (#7506) was opened and its Files changed tab viewed. There is no evidence of opening PR #2 or PR #3, so the core multi-item deliverable is missing. (2) Even for PR #7506, the agent output only reports the file-change summary (files/additions/deletions/tests) and omits multiple required metadata fields: PR number, title, author, last-updated date, and labels. Screenshots show some of these (PR page shows title/number/author and labels “None yet”; PR list shows updated date), so this is an omission, not an unavoidable blocker. (3) The agent did not rank the three PRs by changed-file count, which is impossible to do without inspecting three PRs.\n\nWhat was done correctly: The agent did navigate to the PR list and apply an updated-desc sort via query (q=is:pr is:open sort:updated-desc is visible), and it correctly captured #7506’s Files changed stats: 1 file, 26 additions, 19 deletions, and the only file shown is src/requests/help.py (no test file). Constraint compliance appears fine (no sign-in or modifying actions).\n\nOutcome assessment: From an average user’s perspective, the task is not completed because the primary deliverable—complete reports for the first three qualifying PRs and a ranking among them—is missing. Providing partial details for only one PR is insufficient and would not satisfy the user’s request.",
